"bm25_score\":8.189044968808027,\"bm25_rank\":2,\"vector_distance\":null,\"vector_rank\":null,\"text\":\"3. Construct a decision tree in which each row of the truth table corresponds to one path through the decision tree.\",\"heading_path\":[\"Simple proof:\"],\"scoring_parent_id\":null},{\"chunk_id\":\"cd6684c353e44c7c88e349fccb10f8d0:child:117\",\"rrf_score\":0.015873015873015872,\"rank\":9,\"bm25_score\":7.286611169768634,\"bm25_rank\":3,\"vector_distance\":null,\"vector_rank\":null,\"text\":\"For what number of records does the decision tree's prediction disagree with the true value in the database?\",\"heading_path\":[\"Training Set Error\"],\"scoring_parent_id\":null},{\"chunk_id\":\"cd6684c353e44c7c88e349fccb10f8d0:child:10\",\"rrf_score\":0.015625,\"rank\":10,\"bm25_score\":7.06573537700755,\"bm25_rank\":4,\"vector_distance\":null,\"vector_rank\":null,\"text\":\"Today's lecture\",\"heading_path\":[\"Today's lecture\"],\"scoring_parent_id\":null},{\"chunk_id\":\"cd6684c353e44c7c88e349fccb10f8d0:child:168\",\"rrf_score\":0.015625,\"rank\":11,\"bm25_score\":null,\"bm25_rank\":null,\"vector_distance\":0.415641725063324,\"vector_rank\":4,\"text\":\"Avoiding overfitting\",\"heading_path\":[\"Avoiding overfitting\"],\"scoring_parent_id\":null},{\"chunk_id\":\"cd6684c353e44c7c88e349fccb10f8d0:child:134\",\"rrf_score\":0.015384615384615385,\"rank\":12,\"bm25_score\":6.503193723770157,\"bm25_rank\":5,\"vector_distance\":null,\"vector_rank\":null,\"text\":\"·But once learned, we see how well the tree predicts that data.\",\"heading_path\":[\"Test Set Error\"],\"scoring_parent_id\":null},{\"chunk_id\":\"cd6684c353e44c7c88e349fccb10f8d0:child:257\",\"rrf_score\":0.015384615384615385,\"rank\":13,\"bm25_score\":null,\"bm25_rank\":null,\"vector_distance\":0.417230486869812,\"vector_rank\":5,\"text\":\"· Bayesian Decision Trees can take a different approach to preventing overfitting\",\"heading_path\":[\"What we haven't discussed\"],\"scoring_parent_id\":null},{\"chunk_id\":\"cd6684c353e44c7c88e349fccb10f8d0:child:180\",\"rrf_score\":0.015151515151515152,\"rank\":14,\"bm25_score\":6.492262008229843,\"bm25_rank\":6,\"vector_distance\":null,\"vector_rank\":null,\"text\":\"·Build the full decision tree as before.\",\"heading_path\":[\"Using Chi-squared to avoid overfitting\"],\"scoring_parent_id\":null},{\"chunk_id\":\"cd6684c353e44c7c88e349fccb10f8d0:child:166\",\"rrf_score\":0.014925373134328358,\"rank\":15,\"bm25_score\":null,\"bm25_rank\":null,\"vector_distance\":0.4715529680252075,\"vector_rank\":7,\"text\":\"·Fact (theoretical and empirical): If your machine learning algorithm is overfitting then it may perform less well on test set data.\",\"heading_path\":[\"Overfitting\"],\"scoring_parent_id\":null},{\"chunk_id\":\"cd6684c353e44c7c88e349fccb10f8d0:child:249\",\"rrf_score\":0.014925373134328358,\"rank\":16,\"bm25_score\":6.085284389803495,\"bm25_rank\":7,\"vector_distance\":null,\"vector_rank\":null,\"text\":\"·The recursive algorithm for building an unpruned decision tree\",\"heading_path\":[\"What you should know\"],\"scoring_parent_id\":null},{\"chunk_id\":\"cd6684c353e44c7c88e349fccb10f8d0:child:12\",\"rrf_score\":0.014705882352941176,\"rank\":17,\"bm25_score\":null,\"bm25_rank\":null,\"vector_distance\":0.5034105181694031,\"vector_rank\":8,\"text\":\"·Learning a decision tree classifier from data\",\"heading_path\":[\"Today's lecture\"],\"scoring_parent_id\":null},{\"chunk_id\":\"cd6684c353e44c7c88e349fccb10f8d0:child:182\",\"rrf_score\":0.014492753623188406,\"rank\":18,\"bm25_score\":5.992082001682459,\"bm25_rank\":9,\"vector_distance\":null,\"vector_rank\":null,\"text\":\"·Beginning at the bottom of the tree, delete splits in which pchance> MaxPchance.\",\"heading_path\":[\"Using Chi-squared to avoid overfitting\"],\"scoring_parent_id\":null},{\"chunk_id\":\"cd6684c353e44c7c88e349fccb10f8d0:child:85\",\"rrf_score\":0.014492753623188406,\"rank\":19,\"bm25_score\":null,\"bm25_rank\":null,\"vector_distance\":0.5046699047088623