":[\"Overfitting\"],\"scoring_parent_id\":null},{\"chunk_id\":\"cd6684c353e44c7c88e349fccb10f8d0:child:150\",\"rrf_score\":0.0304147465437788,\"rank\":2,\"bm25_score\":9.75768762602962,\"bm25_rank\":2,\"vector_distance\":0.4933808445930481,\"vector_rank\":10,\"text\":\"Testing the tree with the test set\",\"heading_path\":[\"Testing the tree with the test set\"],\"scoring_parent_id\":null},{\"chunk_id\":\"cd6684c353e44c7c88e349fccb10f8d0:child:251\",\"rrf_score\":0.03007688828584351,\"rank\":3,\"bm25_score\":9.007839996871327,\"bm25_rank\":7,\"vector_distance\":0.46737349033355713,\"vector_rank\":6,\"text\":\"·Why test set errors can be bigger than training set\",\"heading_path\":[\"What you should know\"],\"scoring_parent_id\":null},{\"chunk_id\":\"cd6684c353e44c7c88e349fccb10f8d0:child:252\",\"rrf_score\":0.029857397504456328,\"rank\":4,\"bm25_score\":9.121693265454482,\"bm25_rank\":6,\"vector_distance\":0.47909754514694214,\"vector_rank\":8,\"text\":\"·Why pruning can reduce test set error\",\"heading_path\":[\"What you should know\"],\"scoring_parent_id\":null},{\"chunk_id\":\"cd6684c353e44c7c88e349fccb10f8d0:child:257\",\"rrf_score\":0.029138513513513514,\"rank\":5,\"bm25_score\":8.506552088090555,\"bm25_rank\":14,\"vector_distance\":0.4329589009284973,\"vector_rank\":4,\"text\":\"· Bayesian Decision Trees can take a different approach to preventing overfitting\",\"heading_path\":[\"What we haven't discussed\"],\"scoring_parent_id\":null},{\"chunk_id\":\"cd6684c353e44c7c88e349fccb10f8d0:child:117\",\"rrf_score\":0.028693528693528692,\"rank\":6,\"bm25_score\":9.371528245307509,\"bm25_rank\":3,\"vector_distance\":0.5366171598434448,\"vector_rank\":18,\"text\":\"For what number of records does the decision tree's prediction disagree with the true value in the database?\",\"heading_path\":[\"Training Set Error\"],\"scoring_parent_id\":null},{\"chunk_id\":\"cd6684c353e44c7c88e349fccb10f8d0:child:142\",\"rrf_score\":0.028371628371628373,\"rank\":7,\"bm25_score\":9.29405908983175,\"bm25_rank\":5,\"vector_distance\":0.5365927815437317,\"vector_rank\":17,\"text\":\"·Some y's that were uncorrupted in the training set will be corrupted in the test set.\",\"heading_path\":[\"In our artificial example\"],\"scoring_parent_id\":null},{\"chunk_id\":\"cd6684c353e44c7c88e349fccb10f8d0:child:86\",\"rrf_score\":0.01639344262295082,\"rank\":8,\"bm25_score\":10.704997471015053,\"bm25_rank\":1,\"vector_distance\":null,\"vector_rank\":null,\"text\":\"·A Decision Tree is a tree-structured plan of a set of attributes to test in order to predict the output.\",\"heading_path\":[\"Learning Decision Trees\"],\"scoring_parent_id\":null},{\"chunk_id\":\"cd6684c353e44c7c88e349fccb10f8d0:child:164\",\"rrf_score\":0.016129032258064516,\"rank\":9,\"bm25_score\":null,\"bm25_rank\":null,\"vector_distance\":0.3951927423477173,\"vector_rank\":2,\"text\":\"Overfitting\",\"heading_path\":[\"Overfitting\"],\"scoring_parent_id\":null},{\"chunk_id\":\"cd6684c353e44c7c88e349fccb10f8d0:child:243\",\"rrf_score\":0.015873015873015872,\"rank\":10,\"bm25_score\":null,\"bm25_rank\":null,\"vector_distance\":0.3967130780220032,\"vector_rank\":3,\"text\":\"·It's possible to get in trouble with overfitting\",\"heading_path\":[\"Conclusions\"],\"scoring_parent_id\":null},{\"chunk_id\":\"cd6684c353e44c7c88e349fccb10f8d0:child:152\",\"rrf_score\":0.015625,\"rank\":11,\"bm25_score\":9.308085876717026,\"bm25_rank\":4,\"vector_distance\":null,\"vector_rank\":null,\"text\":\"In total, we expect to be wrong on 3/8 of the test set predictions\\n\\nCopyright ©Andrew W. Moore Slide 63\",\"heading_path\":[\"Testing the tree with the test set\"],\"scoring_parent_id\":null},{\"chunk_id\":\"cd6684c353e44c7c88e349fccb10f8d0:child:165\",\"rrf_score\":0.015384615384615385,\"rank\":12,\"bm25_score\":null,\"bm25_rank\":null,\"vector_distance\":0.4460328221321106,\"vector_rank\":5,\"text\":\"·Definition: If your machine learning algorithm fits noise (i.e. pays attention to parts of the data that are irrelevant) it is overfitting.\",\"heading_path\":[\"Overfitting\"],\"scoring_parent_id\":null},{\"chunk_id\":\"cd6684c353e44c7c88e349fccb10f8d0:child:168\",\"rrf_score\":0.014925373134328358,\"rank\":13,\"bm25_score\":null,\"bm25_rank\":null,\"vector_distance\":0.47140640020370483,\"vector_rank\":7,\"text\":\"Avoiding overfitting\",\"heading_path\":[\"Avoiding overfitting\"],\"scoring_parent_id\":null},{\"chunk_id\":\"cd6684c353e44c7c88e349fccb10f8d0:child:163\",\"rrf_score\":0.014705882352941176,\"rank\":14,\"bm25_score\":8.902546865490764,\"bm25_rank\":8,\"vector_distance\":null,\"vector_rank\":null,\"text\":\"In total, we expect to be wrong on only 1/4 of the test set predictions\\n\\nCopyright ©Andrew W. Moore Slide 68\\n\\n34\",\"heading_path\":[\"Without access to the irrelevant bits…\"],\"scoring_parent_id\":null},{\"chunk_id\":\"cd6684c353e44c7c88e349fccb10f8d0:child:171\",\"rrf_score\":0.014492753623188406,\"rank\":15,\"bm25_score\":null,\"bm25_rank\":null,\"vector_distance\":0.4871978759765625,\"vector_rank\":9,\"text\":\"For example, if y = a AND b then b is an irrelevant variable only in the portion of the tree in which a=0\\n\\nBut we can use simple statistics to warn us that we might be overfitting.\\n\\nCopyright ©Andrew W. Moore Slide 71\\n\\nCopyright ©Andrew W. Moore Slide 72\\n\\n36\",\"heading_path\":[\"Avoiding overfitting\"],\"scoring_parent_id\":null},{\"chunk_id\":\"cd6684c353e44c7c88e349fccb10f8d0:child:211\",\"rrf_score\":0.014492753623188406,\"rank\":16,\"bm25_score\":8.833506597441055,\"bm25_rank\":9,\"vector_distance\":null,\"vector_rank\":null,\"text\":\"Idea One: Branch on each possible real value\\n\\nCopyright ©Andrew W. Moore Slide 82\\n\\nMachine Learning Datasets\\n\\nWhat is Classification?\\n\\nContingency Tables\\n\\nOLAP (Online Analytical Processing)\\n\\nWhat is Data Mining?\\n\\nSearching for High Information Gain\\n\\nLearning an unpruneddecision tree recursively\\n\\nTraining Set Error\\n\\nTest Set Error\\n\\nOverfitting\\n\\nAvoiding Overfitting\\n\\nInformation Gain of a real valued input Building Decision Trees with real Valued Inputs Andrew's homebrewed hack: Binary Categorical Splits Example Decision Trees\\n\\n41\",\"heading_path\":[\"Real-Valued inputs\"],\"scoring_parent_id\":null},{\"chunk_id\":\"cd6684c353e44c7c88e349fccb10f8d0:child:121\",\"rrf_score\":0.014084507042253521,\"rank\":17,\"bm25_score\":8.607023702968077,\"bm25_rank\":11,\"vector_distance\":null,\"vector_rank\":null,\"text\":\"·It is not usually in order to predict the training data's output on data we have already seen.\",\"heading_path\":[\"Stop and reflect: Why are we doing this learning anyway?\"],\"scoring_parent_id\":null},{\"chunk_id\":\"cd6684c353e44c7c88e349fccb10f8d0:child:197\",\"rrf_score\":0.014084507042253521,\"rank\":18,\"bm25_score\":null,\"bm25_rank\":null,\"vector_distance\":0.5061870813369751,\"vector_rank\":11,\"text\":\"·Decision trees are biased to prefer classifiers that can be expressed as trees.\",\"heading_path\":[\"The simplest tree\"],\"scoring_parent_id\":null},{\"chunk_id\":\"cd6684c353e44c7c88e349fccb10f8d0:child:124\",\"rrf_score\":0.013888888888888888,\"rank\":19,\"bm25_score\":8.607023702968077,\"bm25_rank\":12,\"vector_distance\":null,\"vector_rank\":null,\"text\":\"·It is not usually in order to predict the training data's output on data we have already seen.\",\"heading_path\":[\"Stop and reflect: Why are we doing this learning anyway?\"],\"scoring_parent_id\":null},{\"chunk_id\":\"cd6684c353e44c7c88e349fccb10f8d0:child:154\",\"rrf_score\":0.013888888888888888,\"rank\":20,\"bm25_score\":null,\"bm25_rank\":null,\"vector_distance\":0.5184950828552246,\"vector_rank\":12,\"text\":\"·This explains the discrepancy between training and test set error\",\"heading_path\":[\"What's this example shown us?\"],\"scoring_parent_id\":null}],\"matches\":[{\"chunk_id\":\"cd6684c353e44c7c88e349fccb10f8d0:child:166\",\"rrf_score\":0.030679156908665108,\"rank\":1,\"bm25_score\":8.7014795