les\\n\",\"page_indices\":[34]},{\"evidence_id\":\"p9\",\"source_number\":1,\"file_id\":\"cd6684c353e44c7c88e349fccb10f8d0\",\"file_name\":\"decision-trees.pdf\",\"start_offset\":17424,\"end_offset\":17460,\"text\":\"OLAP (Online Analytical Processing)\\n\",\"page_indices\":[34]},{\"evidence_id\":\"p10\",\"source_number\":1,\"file_id\":\"cd6684c353e44c7c88e349fccb10f8d0\",\"file_name\":\"decision-trees.pdf\",\"start_offset\":17461,\"end_offset\":17482,\"text\":\"What is Data Mining?\\n\",\"page_indices\":[34]},{\"evidence_id\":\"p11\",\"source_number\":1,\"file_id\":\"cd6684c353e44c7c88e349fccb10f8d0\",\"file_name\":\"decision-trees.pdf\",\"start_offset\":17483,\"end_offset\":17519,\"text\":\"Searching for High Information Gain\\n\",\"page_indices\":[34]},{\"evidence_id\":\"p12\",\"source_number\":1,\"file_id\":\"cd6684c353e44c7c88e349fccb10f8d0\",\"file_name\":\"decision-trees.pdf\",\"start_offset\":17520,\"end_offset\":17566,\"text\":\"Learning an unpruneddecision tree recursively\\n\",\"page_indices\":[34]},{\"evidence_id\":\"p13\",\"source_number\":1,\"file_id\":\"cd6684c353e44c7c88e349fccb10f8d0\",\"file_name\":\"decision-trees.pdf\",\"start_offset\":17567,\"end_offset\":17586,\"text\":\"Training Set Error\\n\",\"page_indices\":[34]},{\"evidence_id\":\"p14\",\"source_number\":1,\"file_id\":\"cd6684c353e44c7c88e349fccb10f8d0\",\"file_name\":\"decision-trees.pdf\",\"start_offset\":17587,\"end_offset\":17602,\"text\":\"Test Set Error\\n\",\"page_indices\":[34]},{\"evidence_id\":\"p15\",\"source_number\":1,\"file_id\":\"cd6684c353e44c7c88e349fccb10f8d0\",\"file_name\":\"decision-trees.pdf\",\"start_offset\":17603,\"end_offset\":17615,\"text\":\"Overfitting\\n\",\"page_indices\":[34]},{\"evidence_id\":\"p16\",\"source_number\":1,\"file_id\":\"cd6684c353e44c7c88e349fccb10f8d0\",\"file_name\":\"decision-trees.pdf\",\"start_offset\":17616,\"end_offset\":17637,\"text\":\"Avoiding Overfitting\\n\",\"page_indices\":[34]},{\"evidence_id\":\"p17\",\"source_number\":1,\"file_id\":\"cd6684c353e44c7c88e349fccb10f8d0\",\"file_name\":\"decision-trees.pdf\",\"start_offset\":17638,\"end_offset\":17801,\"text\":\"Information Gain of a real valued input Building Decision Trees with real Valued Inputs Andrew's homebrewed hack: Binary Categorical Splits Example Decision Trees\\n\",\"page_indices\":[34]},{\"evidence_id\":\"p18\",\"source_number\":1,\"file_id\":\"cd6684c353e44c7c88e349fccb10f8d0\",\"file_name\":\"decision-trees.pdf\",\"start_offset\":17802,\"end_offset\":17804,\"text\":\"35\",\"page_indices\":[34]},{\"evidence_id\":\"p19\",\"source_number\":2,\"file_id\":\"cd6684c353e44c7c88e349fccb10f8d0\",\"file_name\":\"decision-trees.pdf\",\"start_offset\":17806,\"end_offset\":17827,\"text\":\"Avoiding overfitting\\n\",\"page_indices\":[35]},{\"evidence_id\":\"p20\",\"source_number\":2,\"file_id\":\"cd6684c353e44c7c88e349fccb10f8d0\",\"file_name\":\"decision-trees.pdf\",\"start_offset\":17828,\"end_offset\":17898,\"text\":\"·Usually we do not know in advance which are the irrelevant variables\\n\",\"page_indices\":[35]},{\"evidence_id\":\"p21\",\"source_number\":2,\"file_id\":\"cd6684c353e44c7c88e349fccb10f8d0\",\"file_name\":\"decision-trees.pdf\",\"start_offset\":17899,\"end_offset\":17934,\"text\":\"·…and it may depend on the context\\n\",\"page_indices\":[35]},{\"evidence_id\":\"p22\",\"source_number\":2,\"file_id\":\"cd6684c353e44c7c88e349fccb10f8d0\",\"file_name\":\"decision-trees.pdf\",\"start_offset\":17935,\"end_offset\":18041,\"text\":\"For example, if y = a AND b then b is an irrelevant variable only in the portion of the tree in which a=0\\n\",\"page_indices\":[35]},{\"evidence_id\":\"p23\",\"source_number\":2,\"file_id\":\"cd6684c353e44c7c88e349fccb10f8d0\",\"file_name\":\"decision-trees.pdf\",\"start_offset\":18042,\"end_offset\":18116,\"text\":\"But we can use simple statistics to warn us that we might be overfitting.\\n\",\"page_indices\":[35]},{\"evidence_id\":\"p24\",\"source_number\":2,\"file_id\":\"cd6684c353e44c7c88e349fccb10f8d0\",\"file_name\":\"decision-trees.pdf\",\"start_offset\":18117,\"end_offset\":18153,\"text\":\"Copyright ©Andrew W. Moore Slide 71\\n\",\"page_indices\":[35]},{\"evidence_id\":\"p25\",\"source_number\":2,\"file_id\":\"cd6684c353e44c7c88e349fccb10f8d0\",\"file_name\":\"decision-trees.pdf\",\"start_offset\":18154,\"end_offset\":18190,\"text\":\"Copyright ©Andrew W. Moore Slide 72\\n\",\"page_indices\":[35]},{\"evidence_id\":\"p26\",\"source_number\":2,\"file_id\":\"cd6684c353e44c7c88e349fccb10f8d0\",\"file_name\":\"decision-trees.pdf\",\"start_offset\":18191,\"end_offset\":18193,\"text\":\"36\",\"page_indices\":[35]},{\"evidence_id\":\"p27\",\"source_number\":3,\"file_id\":\"cd6684c353e44c7c88e349fccb10f8d0\",\"file_name\":\"decision-trees.pdf\",\"start_offset\":25299,\"end_offset\":25325,\"text\":\"What we haven't discussed\\n\",\"page_indices\":[49]},{\"evidence_id\":\"p28\",\"source_number\":3,\"file_id\":\"cd6684c353e44c7c88e349fccb10f8d0\",\"file_name\":\"decision-trees.pdf\",\"start_offset\":25326,\"end_offset\":25407,\"text\":\"· It's easy to have real-valued outputs too---these are called Regression Trees*\\n\",\"page_indices\":[49]},{\"evidence_id\":\"p29\",\"source_number\":3,\"file_id\":\"cd6684c353e44c7c88e349fccb10f8d0\",\"file_name\":\"decision-trees.pdf\",\"start_offset\":25408,\"end_offset\":25490,\"text\":\"· Bayesian Decision Trees can take a different approach to preventing overfitting\\n\",\"page_indices\":[49]},{\"evidence_id\":\"p30\",\"source_number\":3,\"file_id\":\"cd6684c353e44c7c88e349fccb10f8d0\",\"file_name\":\"decision-trees.pdf\",\"start_offset\":25491,\"end_offset\":25548,\"text\":\"· Computational complexity (straightforward and cheap) *\\n\",\"page_indices\":[49]},{\"evidence_id\":\"p31\",\"source_number\":3,\"file_id\":\"cd6684c353e44c7c88e349fccb10f8d0\",\"file_name\":\"decision-trees.pdf\",\"start_offset\":25549,\"end_offset\":25604,\"text\":\"· Alternatives to Information Gain for splitting nodes\\n\",\"page_indices\":[49]},{\"evidence_id\":\"p32\",\"source_number\":3,\"file_id\":\"cd6684c353e44c7c88e349fccb10f8d0\",\"file_name\":\"decision-trees.pdf\",\"start_offset\":25605,\"end_offset\":25648,\"text\":\"· How to choose MaxPchance automatically *\\n\",\"page_indices\":[49]},{\"evidence_id\":\"p33\",\"source_number\":3,\"file_id\":\"cd6684c353e44c7c88e349fccb10f8d0\",\"file_name\":\"decision-trees.pdf\",\"start_offset\":25649,\"end_offset\":25688,\"text\":\"· The details of Chi-Squared testing *\\n\",\"page_indices\":[49]},{\"evidence_id\":\"p34\",\"source_number\":3,\"file_id\":\"cd6684c353e44c7c88e349fccb10f8d0\",\"file_name\":\"decision-trees.pdf\",\"start_offset\":25689,\"end_offset\":25737,\"text\":\"· Boosting---a simple way to improve accuracy *\\n\",\"page_indices\":[49]},{\"evidence_id\":\"p35\",\"source_number\":3,\"file_id\":\"cd6684c353e44c7c88e349fccb10f8d0\",\"file_name\":\"decision-trees.pdf\",\"start_offset\":25738,\"end_offset\":25777,\"text\":\"* = discussed in other Andrew lectures\\n\",\"page_indices\":[49]},{\"evidence_id\":\"p36\",\"source_number\":3,\"file_id\":\"cd6684c353e44c7c88e349fccb10f8d0\",\"file_name\":\"decision-trees.pdf\",\"start_offset\":25778,\"end_offset\":25813,\"text\":\"Copyright ©Andrew W. Moore Slide 99\",\"page_indices\":[49]}],\"record\":{\"prompt_version\":\"evidence-sufficiency-v6\",\"requested_model\":\"gpt-4.1\",\"model\":\"gpt-4.1-2025-04-14\",\"response_id\":\"resp_0002c7d3e5231bc9006abe83704e4887d28110cebdb1fa1fbe\",\"output_text\":\"{\\n  \\\"requirements\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"requirement_id\\\": \\\"R1\\\",\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"supported\\\",\\n      \\\"gap\\\": \\\"\\\",\\n      \\\"references\\\": [\\n        {\\n          \\\"evidence_id\\\": \\\"p2\\\"\\n        }\\n      ]\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"requirement_id\\\": \\\"R2\\\",\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"supported\\\",\\n      \\\"gap\\\": \\\"\\\",\\n      \\\"references\\\": [\\n        {\\n          \\\"evidence_id\\\": \\\"p3\\\"\\n        }\\n      ]\\